+| Intent versus known error | DOT report physical p2 result 1 says insufficient evidence of knowing falsehood/omission/intentional failure to correct **regarding notifications to DOD**. Physical p10 separately says three executives learned a liaison-answer error and none informed the Commission. Current pins P09–P10 retain both. | Contemporaneous knowledge, instruction and decision records; intent cannot be inferred solely from noncorrection. |
+| Awareness and assignment | Report p10 describes possible same-day knowledge, a conversation within weeks, and another by summer's end. Executives expected others/the liaison to correct; liaison said nobody asked her and she did not do so. P10; prior interview pins retain their differing testimony. | Original drafts, assignment/clearance emails, correction instruction/delivery and interview audio. No harmonized awareness date selected. |
+| Drafting responsibility | The earlier publication preserves Schuessler's Miller/Osmus attribution beside Miller's denial and Osmus's account of Brown typing/Schuessler providing phone information. These are retrospective accounts, not an authenticated draft history. | The actual 2003 native drafts, attachments, edit chain and transmittal. Prior FC02–FC04 and R01 remain open. |
