+# Search, preservation and limits
+
+Public primary sources and previously held public releases only; no private case correspondence or personal mailbox access. Original research, official findings, derivative reporting, possible record routes and hypotheses are labeled separately. No legal claim or litigation record is altered.
+
+The search pursued case-specific post-August2006 correction, administrative-action/no-action and recommendation-disposition records. Exact and variant report IDs, QFR terms, executive/action terms, official FAA/DOT/OIG pages, their linked annual/semiannual reports and historical records/audit directives were checked. SEARCH-QUERIES.json is the retained explicit query list; it is not a claim of exhaustiveness. Search-engine dates are not treated as document issue dates. Reprints of the same newspaper/wire account are not independent corroboration. No final case-specific disposition was located.
+
+Eight new official PDFs and an FAA order-index HTML response were successfully preserved with URL, UTC access time, content type, bytes and SHA-256. Six initial FAA HTTP200 acquisitions could not be saved because the new Intel study subdirectory did not exist. The original failure ledger remains; the directory was created only after verifying the media parent, and a separately recorded retry acquired all six. This was a workflow error, not an archive anomaly. Public ACCESS-RESULTS.json keeps the failure categories without private local paths. Acquisition scripts/complete ledgers remain in the native study.
+
+Four report PDFs and the DOT library URL returned HTTP403 during fresh direct retrieval; their five 162-byte response bodies and common hash remain preserved. The web tool could parse the library page/report material. These are different access observations, not proof of suppression, removal or an original-payload change. Earlier successful original DOT bytes remain held. No fresh PDF page-version comparison was possible and no edition change is claimed.
+
+All pages of the eight new PDFs were text-extracted using pypdf6.10.0 on Python3.13.7. Case locators in the181-page FY2006 and182-page FY2007 FAA reports were repeated and saved, not promoted to exhaustive review. Substring searches are sensitive to OCR, line-breaks, spacing and vocabulary. Neither annual report is established as a complete recommendation register. Previously web-parsed2006/2007 OIG semiannual material was an exploratory lead; direct originals remained inaccessible. This pass does not claim a new complete semiannual-table review or reinterpret earlier search failures as absence of action.
+
+Seventeen selected pages were rendered with pdftoppm and viewed: new schedule tables, old audit-order scope/custody fields, the2001 checklist, the2013 replacement, the prior case's closure fields/synopsis, one article locator and report results/recommendations. VISUAL-REVIEW.json identifies the pages. Source-text pins are exact extraction substrings with within-page line numbers; manual image transcriptions are explicitly separate. OCR `MA-1` remains in P06 and image `AAA-1` in V03. Copies/hashes establish byte identity, not factual correctness or native-email authenticity.
+
+Prepublication review caught an erroneous draft comparison that stopped at report p12: recommendations 3 and 4 continue on p13. That continuation was extracted and visually checked; the unsupported discrepancy was removed before publication. The unpublished first draft and its exact revision diff remain in the native study. P14 retains the continuation; no underlying source was changed.
+
+This publication is a new directory. Prior publications, original response bodies, private coordination and the master register are unchanged. The public payload contains research notes, public-source descriptors, limited quoted/extracted passages and integrity tooling; large originals/rasters and internal chat coordination remain in their separate research stores. The third-party article is linked and briefly summarized, not republished. No native FAA statement, administrative decision or correction receipt is claimed recovered. No outreach, fees, submission, deletion or history rewrite occurred.
